   "notes": "ROLLING ORDER: Upper A \u2192 Lower A \u2192 Upper B \u2192 Lower B. Typical week: Mon, Tue, Wed, Fri. THURSDAY IS ALWAYS REST (Friday-morning quiz). Missed a day? Do the next session in order; never double up.\nSupersets are used ONLY where both moves share the same bench, dumbbells, rope, or machine so you never wait or carry gear. Rest timer = rest after the SECOND move. Anything marked straight sets: finish all sets, rest the listed time.\nEffort: 1\u20132 reps in reserve on compounds; last set of isolations 0\u20131. Progression: when every set hits the TOP of the range at \u22642 RIR, add 2.5\u20135 lb.\nTime cap: if you're past ~50 min, trim the last pair to 2 rounds.\n\nSS A (2 min): incline DB press + chest-supported DB row\u2014same incline bench and dumbbells (set bench ~30\u201345\u00b0), antagonist pair, no interference.\nPull-ups: straight sets, 2 min rest. Add weight when you reach 3\u00d710 at bodyweight.\nSS B (75 sec): DB lateral raise + DB curl\u2014same dumbbell rack.\nSS C (60 sec): face pull + overhead triceps extension\u2014same rope on the same cable tower.\n~21 sets.",
