  {
   "id": "plan-joey-c6-lower-a",
   "name": "2: Lower A \u2014 Glutes, Adductors & Leg Press (~45 min)",
   "folderId": "folder-joey-c6",
   "notes": "ROLLING ORDER: Upper A \u2192 Lower A \u2192 Upper B \u2192 Lower B. Typical week: Mon, Tue, Wed, Fri. THURSDAY IS ALWAYS REST (Friday-morning quiz). Missed a day? Do the next session in order; never double up.\nSupersets are used ONLY where both moves share the same bench, dumbbells, rope, or machine so you never wait or carry gear. Rest timer = rest after the SECOND move. Anything marked straight sets: finish all sets, rest the listed time.\nEffort: 1\u20132 reps in reserve on compounds; last set of isolations 0\u20131. Progression: when every set hits the TOP of the range at \u22642 RIR, add 2.5\u20135 lb.\nTime cap: if you're past ~50 min, trim the last pair to 2 rounds.\nKNEE (right, patellofemoral pain): wear your sleeve. Pain should stay \u22643/10, never sharp, and settle back to baseline within 24 h; if not, drop the weight or range next time. Squat/press only to a pain-free depth (about 60\u201370\u00b0 knee bend), controlled tempo, no bouncing. Persistent or worsening pain: get it assessed (sports med/PT) instead of pushing through.\n\nWarm-up: wall sit at ~60\u00b0 (isometric knee prep, 2\u00d730\u201345 sec) before the leg press.\nSS A (2 min): leg press (shallow, pain-free range, feet a bit high and wide) + leg press calf raise\u2014same machine. Start ~20% lighter than your full-range weight.\nHip thrust: straight sets, 2 min. Barbell with pad, or machine/Smith. Pause 1 sec at the top.\nSS B (75 sec): hip adduction + hip abduction\u2014usually the same machine (flip the pads) or neighbouring ones.\nSeated leg curl, 3 straight sets, 75 sec.\nCable crunch, 2 straight sets, 60 sec.\n~21 sets.",
